/-!
# Ambient normalization: normal-cover reduction

The source configuration constructs a normal containing C-component D, places
Lᵥ in D using its noncentral projection, and realizes K as a radical supplement
in D. Quasisimplicity of D/O₂(D) completes that branch. Normalization in the
remaining branch lifts from D/O₂(D), with the literal kernel and its action
on K proved in `NormalCover`.

The exceptional odd-radical rigidity and the universal A.3.8/A.3.12 inputs
remain source obligations. No unconditional ambient-normalization theorem is
asserted here. Source: Aschbacher–Smith, 13.6.20, printed p.931.
-/
